UID:ec4f4874878f26c4@role-healthcare-human-services.maine-government-feeds
DTSTAMP:20261026T223919Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261026
SUMMARY:[Curated Role Feeds] US Department of Labor awards $250\,000 in Br
 ookwood-Sago Grants to promote mine safety\, health education
DESCRIPTION:WASHINGTON – The U.S. Department of Labor today announced th
 e award of $250\,000 in Brookwood-Sago grant funding to two organizations 
 to support education and training initiatives that will help identify and 
 prevent unsafe working conditions in and around the nation’s mines.Admin
 istered by the department’s Mine Safety and Health Administration\, the
  Brookwood-Sago Mine Safety grant program helps recipients create trainin
 g materials\, conduct mine safety training\, and educational programs desi
 gned to protect the safety and health of miners. In awarding the grants\,
  MSHA focused on innovative plans for mine safety and pilot programs that 
 may be useful for miners working in a broad range of positions. The grants
  also put an emphasis on programs and materials targeting workers in small
 er mines that train mine operators and miners about MSHA standards\, and e
 mergency response training.Established under the Mine Improvement and New
  Emergency Response Act of 2006\, the grant program honors the miners los
 t at the Jim Walter Resources #5 mine in Brookwood\, Alabama\, on Sept. 23
 \, 2001\, and at the Sago Mine in Buckhannon\, West Virginia\, on Jan. 2\,
  2006.The recipients of the 2026 Brookwood-Sago grants are as follows:Reci
 pientCityState/TerritoryAmountSaelua Medical Corporation Pago PagoAmerica
 n Samoa$170\,000University of ArizonaTucsonAZ$80\,000\nhttp://www.dol.gov/
 newsroom/releases/msha/msha20261026
URL:http://www.dol.gov/newsroom/releases/msha/msha20261026
CATEGORIES:Curated Role Feeds
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:b5ff73af40e3d3dc@role-healthcare-human-services.maine-government-feeds
DTSTAMP:20261023T113402Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261023
SUMMARY:[Curated Role Feeds] National Vaccine Injury Compensation Program\
 ; List of Petitions Received
DESCRIPTION:HRSA is publishing this notice of petitions received under the
  National Vaccine Injury Compensation Program (the Program)\, as required 
 by the Public Health Service (PHS) Act\, as amended. While the Secretary o
 f HHS is named as the respondent in all proceedings brought by the filing 
 of petitions for compensation under the Program\, the United States Court 
 of Federal Claims is charged by statute with responsibility for considerin
 g and acting upon the petitions.\nhttps://www.federalregister.gov/document
 s/2026/10/23/2026-21672/national-vaccine-injury-compensation-program-list-
 of-petitions-received
URL:https://www.federalregister.gov/documents/2026/10/23/2026-21672/nation
 al-vaccine-injury-compensation-program-list-of-petitions-received
CATEGORIES:Curated Role Feeds
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
