UID:0682e47d62e4f8d5@role-healthcare-human-services.maine-government-feeds
DTSTAMP:20261013T224142Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261013
SUMMARY:[Curated Role Feeds] Massage Therapy Awareness Week - October 25 t
 hrough 31
DESCRIPTION:WHEREAS\n\, years of research have demonstrated the effectiven
 ess of massage therapy in a wide range of health treatments\, including pa
 in relief\, management of cancer symptoms\, reduction of depression\, and 
 overall enhancement of physical and mental well-being\; and\nWHEREAS\n\, m
 any individuals recognize the benefits of massage therapy for their health
  and turn to massage as a vital component of their health care regimen\; a
 nd\nWHEREAS\n\, Massage Therapy Awareness Week provides an opportunity for
  massage therapists across Maine to promote the health benefits of their p
 ractice and raise awareness in their communities about the essential role 
 massage therapy plays in maintaining and improving health\; and\nWHEREAS\n
 \, there are over 3\,000 licensed massage therapists serving the people of
  Maine and a dozen pre-approved massage therapy schools in Maine\; and\nWH
 EREAS\n\, Massage Therapy Awareness Week serves as a reminder of the impor
 tance of holistic approaches to health\, and the significant contributions
  of massage therapists in helping people live healthier\, more balanced li
 ves\;\nNOW\, THEREFORE\n\, be it resolved that I\, Janet T. Mills\, Govern
 or of the State of Maine\, do hereby proclaim the week of October 25-31\, 
 2026\, as\nMassage Therapy Awareness Week\nthroughout the State of Maine\,
  and I urge all citizens to recognize this observance.\nIn testimony where
 of\, I have caused\nthe Great Seal of the State to be\nhereunto affixed GI
 VEN under my\nhand at Augusta this eighth day of\nOctober Two Thousand Twe
 nty-Six\nhttp://www.maine.gov/governor/mills/official_documents/proclamati
 ons/2026-10-massage-therapy-awareness-week-october-25-through-31
URL:http://www.maine.gov/governor/mills/official_documents/proclamations/2
 026-10-massage-therapy-awareness-week-october-25-through-31
CATEGORIES:Curated Role Feeds
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:8eaee101f5227860@role-healthcare-human-services.maine-government-feeds
DTSTAMP:20261013T224142Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261013
SUMMARY:[Curated Role Feeds] Blindness Awareness Month - October
DESCRIPTION:WHEREAS\,\nblindness and low vision affect millions of America
 ns\, including an estimated 35\,000 Maine people\; and\nWHEREAS\,\nthe whi
 te cane and guide dog serve as essential tools that promote independence\,
  mobility\, and safety for people who are blind or have low vision\, and M
 aine law recognizes their use and provides protections for people who use 
 them\; and\nWHEREAS\,\npeople who are blind and or low vision contribute s
 ignificantly to the social\, cultural\, and economic vitality of our state
  as they pursue meaningful careers in diverse professions\, strengthen Mai
 ne's workforce\, raise families\, and enrich our communities through their
  participation in all aspects of life\; and\nWHEREAS\,\nwe honor the resil
 ience\, wisdom\, and lifelong contributions of older adults who are blind 
 or have low vision\, and their efforts to maintain independence while navi
 gating the unique challenges of aging with vision loss\; and\nWHEREAS\,\np
 eople with vision loss continue to encounter stigma\, discrimination\, and
  accessibility barriers\, including misconceptions about their capabilitie
 s and needs\; and\nWHEREAS\,\nwe recognize the efforts of vision rehabilit
 ation professionals\, educators\, self-advocates\, and allies across Maine
  who work to advance equality\, accessibility and opportunities for people
  who are blind or have low vision\; and\nWHEREAS\,\nBlindness Awareness Mo
 nth calls attention to the importance of accessibility\, inclusion\, and r
 espect\, and reminds us of the progress achieved through advocacy\, educat
 ion\, and civil rights protections\, as well as the work still to be done\
 ;\nNOW\, THEREFORE\,\nbe it resolved that I\, Janet T. Mills\, Governor of
  the State of Maine\, do hereby proclaim October 2026 as\nBlindness Awaren
 ess Month\nin Maine\, and I call upon all residents to join in recognizing
  the contributions of Maine people who are blind or have low vision and to
  work together to promote accessibility\, inclusion\, independence\, and f
 ull participation in all aspects of community life.\nIn testimony whereof\
 , I have\nhttp://www.maine.gov/governor/mills/official_documents/proclamat
 ions/2026-10-blindness-awareness-month-october
URL:http://www.maine.gov/governor/mills/official_documents/proclamations/2
 026-10-blindness-awareness-month-october
CATEGORIES:Curated Role Feeds
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
