UID:15df90ca2456269e@role-healthcare-human-services.maine-government-feeds
DTSTAMP:20261013T140732Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261013
SUMMARY:[Curated Role Feeds] System Remittance Advice (RA) and 835 Limitat
 ions
DESCRIPTION:Maine.gov\nAgencies\n|\nOnline Services\n|\nHelp\n|\nSearch Ma
 ine.gov\nDHHS\n→\nOffice of MaineCare Services (OMS)\n→\nProvider Reso
 urces\n→\n	 \n			System Remittance Advice (RA) and 835 Limitations\nSyst
 em Remittance Advice (RA) and 835 Limitations\nOct 13\, 2026\nAttention Nu
 rsing Homes\, Hospitals\, and Private Non-Medical Institutions\, Appendix 
 C & F (PNMI-C-F): Claims RA/835 Issues\nFollowing the\nMIHMS upgrade\n\, t
 here are open issues affecting some RA/835s.  The issues are high priori
 ty for a fix that is underway\; we are currently targeting to fix the issu
 es by the end of October and will send another communication when the issu
 es have been resolved. This message provides details of the issues and ava
 ilable workarounds until the issues are fixed.\nCost of Care Reporting for
  Nursing Home\, Hospital Claims\, and PNMI-C-F\nNursing Home and Hospital 
 claims for members with cost of care are not being reported with the appro
 priate Claim Adjustment Reason Code (CARC) needed for balance billing memb
 ers.\nPDF RA – CARC 142 is not being reported for cost of care.\n835 –
  CARC 96 is being reported in error.\nAs a workaround until the fix is in 
 place\, MaineCare will provide a report that can be accessed on the\nMaine
 Care Partner Portal\n. On the Dashboard\, navigate to Reports > Other Repo
 rts > “Cost of Care Report.” This report will be available on Mondays 
 for the claims finalized on the prior Wednesday. Because this week’s cla
 ims will be finalized on Thursday\, the first report will be available no 
 later than Tuesday\, October 20\, 2026.\nSpenddown Reporting for Provider 
 Claims\nClaims with spenddown are not being reported with the appropriate 
 CARC needed for balance billing members.\nPDF RA – CARC 142 is not being
  reported for spenddown claims.\n835 – CARC 96 and/or CARC 178 is being 
 reported in error.\nAs a workaround until the fix is in place\, MaineCare 
 will provide a report that can be accessed on the MaineCare Partner Portal
 . On the dashboard\, navigate to Reports > Other Reports > “Spend Down R
 eport.” This\nhttps://www.maine.gov/dhhs/oms/providers/provider-bulletin
 s/system-remittance-advice-ra-and-835-limitations-2026-10-13
URL:https://www.maine.gov/dhhs/oms/providers/provider-bulletins/system-rem
 ittance-advice-ra-and-835-limitations-2026-10-13
CATEGORIES:Curated Role Feeds
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:7adede86b9446278@role-healthcare-human-services.maine-government-feeds
DTSTAMP:20261012T151652Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261012
SUMMARY:[Curated Role Feeds] Attention Trading Partners: the MaineCare Par
 tner Portal is Live
DESCRIPTION:Maine.gov\nAgencies\n|\nOnline Services\n|\nHelp\n|\nSearch Ma
 ine.gov\nDHHS\n→\nOffice of MaineCare Services (OMS)\n→\nProvider Reso
 urces\n→\n	 \n			Attention Trading Partners: the MaineCare Partner Porta
 l is Live\nAttention Trading Partners: the MaineCare Partner Portal is Liv
 e\nOct 12\, 2026\nAs an update to\nprevious communications\n\, we have lau
 nched the new\nMaineCare Partner Portal\n\, which replaces the previous He
 althPAS Online Portal. The MaineCare Partner Portal is now available for a
 ll regular functions\, 24 hours a day\, 7 days a week.\nAs a\nreminder\n\,
  starting today\, we are also changing how callers interact with and exper
 ience Provider Services and Member Services call center phone menus\, know
 n as Interactive Voice Response (IVR). A virtual assistant\, called Gabby\
 , will replace traditional phone menus by listening to what callers say to
  resolve simple inquiries.\nThis message includes information you will nee
 d to get started in the MaineCare Partner Portal. The link to the MaineCar
 e Partner Portal has not changed:\nmainecare.maine.gov\n.\nFor all informa
 tion about the upcoming changes to MIHMS\, see the MaineCare Partner Porta
 l section of the\nProvider Resources\npage. Please note that we have updat
 ed the\nFAQ\npreviously shared\, as of September 21\, 2026. For informat
 ion about the claims submission deadlines for the October 15\, 2026 and Oc
 tober 21\, 2026\, payment cycles\, please refer to the FAQ.\nMigrated Trad
 ing Partner Account Admin (R7) users\nComplete a one-time self-service pas
 sword reset. Click “Sign In” within the\nMaineCare Partner Portal\n\, 
 then click “Forgot Password” to reset your password. The “Forgot you
 r password?” feature is now a self-service tool! Provider Services will 
 not be able to assist with password resets.\nSet up a\nMulti-Factor Authen
 tication (MFA) method\n.\nSign into MaineCare’s Partner Portal.\nInvite 
 additional (delegated) users and assign permissions as appropriate. Refer 
 to the MaineCare Partner Portal Overview User Guide in the\nMMIS Learning 
 Center\n.\nFind step-by-s\nhttps://www.maine.gov/dhhs/oms/providers/provid
 er-bulletins/attention-trading-partners-mainecare-partner-portal-live-2026
 -10-12
URL:https://www.maine.gov/dhhs/oms/providers/provider-bulletins/attention-
 trading-partners-mainecare-partner-portal-live-2026-10-12
CATEGORIES:Curated Role Feeds
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
