UID:848ccab914fa9fc8@role-healthcare-human-services.maine-government-feeds
DTSTAMP:20261009T223646Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261009
SUMMARY:[Curated Role Feeds] MaineCare Coverage of Gender-Affirming Care f
 or Medicaid Beneficiaries Under Age 18 and Children's Health Insurance Pro
 gram (CHIP) Enrollees Under Age 19
DESCRIPTION:Maine.gov\nAgencies\n|\nOnline Services\n|\nHelp\n|\nSearch Ma
 ine.gov\nDHHS\n→\nOffice of MaineCare Services (OMS)\n→\nProvider Reso
 urces\n→\n	 \n			MaineCare Coverage of Gender-Affirming Care for Medicai
 d Beneficiaries Under Age 18 and Children's Health Insurance Program (CHIP
 ) Enrollees Under Age 19\nMaineCare Coverage of Gender-Affirming Care for 
 Medicaid Beneficiaries Under Age 18 and Children's Health Insurance Progra
 m (CHIP) Enrollees Under Age 19\nOct 09\, 2026\nAs described in the messag
 e sent\nSeptember 18\, 2026\n\, the Centers for Medicare & Medicaid Servic
 es (CMS) published a final rule in the Federal Register on August 13\, 202
 6\, that limits federal Medicaid and CHIP funding for certain gender-affir
 ming care provided to minors. This rule prohibits federal matching funds f
 or puberty blockers\, cross-sex hormone therapy\, and surgical interventio
 ns when used for gender transition for Medicaid beneficiaries under age 18
  and CHIP enrollees under age 19. The federal rule is scheduled to take ef
 fect on October 13\, 2026.\nThe federal rule does not prohibit states from
  using state-only funds to cover these services. Maine\nlaw\nrequires Main
 eCare to cover medically necessary treatment for or related to gender dysp
 horia and protects members from discrimination based on gender identity or
  gender expression.\nTo ensure we are in compliance with this new federal 
 rule\, we have established the billing requirements below for providers wh
 o deliver gender-affirming care services to Medicaid beneficiaries under a
 ge 18 and CHIP enrollees under age 19.\nEffective on October 13\, 2026\, m
 edical claims submitted through the MIHMS system must:\nInclude applicable
  gender-affirming care diagnosis codes on all claims.\nInclude the SE modi
 fier on any claims submitted for gender-affirming care\, other than behavi
 oral health services.\nThe SE modifier is used to identify a service that 
 must be reimbursed using state-only funds.\nThe SE modifier should be list
 ed after any other modifiers on the applicable claim line(s).\nhttps://www
 .maine.gov/dhhs/oms/providers/provider-bulletins/mainecare-coverage-gender
 -affirming-care-medicaid-beneficiaries-under-age-18-and-childrens
URL:https://www.maine.gov/dhhs/oms/providers/provider-bulletins/mainecare-
 coverage-gender-affirming-care-medicaid-beneficiaries-under-age-18-and-chi
 ldrens
CATEGORIES:Curated Role Feeds
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:1788c837d1cf5798@role-healthcare-human-services.maine-government-feeds
DTSTAMP:20261009T223613Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261009
SUMMARY:[Curated Role Feeds] Saving Money on Winter Heating Costs
DESCRIPTION:Hello\, this is Governor Janet Mills\, and thank you for liste
 ning.\nWell\, it's getting more and more painful to fill up at a gas stati
 on or fill a tank of oil to heat your home. And we all know why.\nLook\, w
 e're making progress shifting to other sources of energy to heat our homes
 \, but we're still the most dependent on heating oil to heat our homes in 
 the in the entire country. That reliance on heating oil makes us vulnerabl
 e to great shifts in global energy markets that drive up costs for Maine p
 eople and businesses. This president's war in Iran right now has created t
 he largest fuel supply disruption in global history and has driven energy 
 prices to record highs. The price of heating oil in Maine has reached more
  than $6 a gallon\, so you'll be paying almost $800 more to fill a standar
 d 275 gallon tank than you did a year ago. Kerosene prices are also reachi
 ng historic highs\, all because of this war.\nMaine people should not be f
 orced to choose between staying warm or putting food on the table because 
 the president chose to drag us into a needless war -- and an endless war\,
  it appears.\nMy administration is doing what it can to help people save m
 oney on heating costs and stay comfortable in their homes this winter.\nIt
 's not enough\, but I've directed the Department of Health and Human Servi
 ces to identify households that would be eligible for $40 million in disco
 unts on their electric bills through Maine's Low Income Assistance Program
 \, or LIAP. Starting in November\, thousands of eligible families who are 
 customers of CMP or Versant will begin to see discounts ranging from 20 pe
 rcent to 80 percent\, and these will be applied automatically every month 
 to their electric bills. It's one thing we can do. Families who already ge
 t federal assistance for home heating oil through LIHEAP\, the Low Income 
 Energy Assistance Program\, will also be enrolled automatically in this st
 ate assistance program\, LIAP\, to get the maximum savings on their electr
 ic bills without any unnecessary pa\nhttp://www.maine.gov/governor/mills/n
 ews/radio_address/saving-money-winter-heating-costs-2026-10-09
URL:http://www.maine.gov/governor/mills/news/radio_address/saving-money-wi
 nter-heating-costs-2026-10-09
CATEGORIES:Curated Role Feeds
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
